	(text "PLL: ADF4002 locks the 32 MHz VCXO to REF_10M.\nR = 50, N = 160, PFD 200 kHz. VCXO Kv = 85 ppm/V (2.7 kHz/V).\nLoop filter, all C0G: ICP 1.25 mA gives about 58 Hz loop\nbandwidth and 63 deg phase margin.\nICP 0.625 mA to 5 mA gives 32 Hz to 200 Hz.\nR42/R43 hold VC at mid supply when CP is in three-state.\nRFIN: 470R and 49R9 reduce the 3.3 V CMOS\nsignal to about -7 dBm."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 264.16 121.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0b7be9bb-c964-4396-930a-65c6564800c8")
	)
	(text "RX step attenuators: 3x PE4312 in series, 0 dB to 94.5 dB in 0.5 dB steps.\nSerial mode (P/S high). All C inputs high: 31.5 dB in each attenuator at power up.\nThe SPI bus is shared. Keep ATT_LE1 to ATT_LE3 low when you do not write to an attenuator."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 46.99 253.746 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1e223219-1feb-46b7-8e88-87b45a2a49ba")
	)
	(text "Preliminary M.2 key E pinout (standard names in brackets)\n\nUsed now:\n  8 I2S_BCLK (PCM_CLK), 10 I2S_WS (PCM_SYNC)\n  12 I2S_RX (PCM_IN), 14 I2S_TX (PCM_OUT)\n  9 SPI_SCK (SDIO_CLK), 11 SPI_MOSI (SDIO_CMD)\n  13 SPI_MISO (SDIO_DATA0), 15 SX_CS (SDIO_DATA1)\n  23 SX_RESET (SDIO_RESET), 38 ID_SD, 40 ID_SC (VENDOR_DEFINED)\n  17 ATT_LE1 (SDIO_DATA2), 19 ATT_LE2 (SDIO_DATA3), 54 ATT_LE3 (W_DISABLE2)\n  56 PLL_LE (W_DISABLE1), 62 PLL_MUXOUT (ALERT), 50 REF_10M (SUSCLK)\n  71, 73 +5V (RESERVED, not standard): TX amplifier\n\nReserved:\n  44 PPS (COEX3)\n  58 I2C_SDA, 60 I2C_SCL (no pull-ups on the card)\n  22 UART_RX, 32 UART_TX"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110.49 25.146 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3bbe54db-4bfa-40ec-a1c7-078979d20a89")
	)
	(text "M.2 key E card connector. Preliminary pinout."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.1 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "79641211-d1e4-4e22-b5f6-64868c244511")
	)
	(text "TX: SX1255 RFO_P, HMC374 driver from +5V (90 mA), U.FL.\nMatch for 420-450 MHz (simulated: 14.4 dB gain,\nreturn loss > 15 dB, stable).\n\nL23 has the DC block C77, so no DC reaches the RFIN pin.\n400-510 MHz version (11.2 dB): fit R46 220R, C78 15p and C82 1p,\nchange C76 to 6.8p, R47 to 100R and C81 to 100p."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 272.034 199.39 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7e03605c-19c2-4383-ac66-3aa6d39ad34a")
	)
	(text "${WIP_MARK}"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 409.84 12.7 0)
		(effects
